   "answer": "The review found two numbers with no logged source. I removed both. I also checked the outlier claim with a script, and the script output is now in the log. The corrected answer follows.\n\n**What I did**\n1. Ranked the 15 candidate genes over all 44 samples with geNorm and NormFinder, without groups (rank_reference_genes).\n2. Reran NormFinder with the samples grouped by tissue (E, H, FL) (rank_reference_genes).\n3. Ran geNorm on the 11 head (H) samples only (rank_reference_genes).\n4. Fitted the slope and efficiency of each gene from the dilution series (fit_efficiency).\n5. Checked the sample count per tissue and the outlier flags with a script. The script removed nothing.\n\n**Data and settings**\n- One replicate is one embryo sample. Each sample has one Cq per gene, so no technical replicates were averaged.\n- Samples per tissue: E 24, H 11, FL 9. Total 44. Confirmed by the script.\n- No Cq cutoff was applied. There were 0 non-detects and 0 excluded wells.\n- The stability ranking used efficiency 2 for every gene. This is the tool default in that run.\n- The NormqPCR version is 1.58.0. The tool results do not give the R version.\n\n**Outlier check (my script, not removed)**\n- With all genes pooled within each tissue, the modified z-score rule (above 3.5) flags 44 Cq values. The script reproduced this count.\n- With each gene checked alone within its tissue, 7 values are flagged. These are RPL13a in H (2 wells), HPRT1 in H (1 well), UBC in H (1 well), and B2M in H (3 wells).\n- Inference: the pooled count of 44 falls to 7 per gene. So most of the pooled flags reflect differences between genes. Seven flags remain, all in the head group of 11 samples.\n- All values stayed in the analysis.\n\n**geNorm, all 44 samples (15 genes)**\n- Best pair: HTATSF1 and CDC40. Average M = 0.2175.\n- Average M with the least stable gene (HPRT1) still in the set (15 genes): 0.5275.\n- Average M with the two least stable genes (HPRT1 and B2M) removed (13 genes): 0.4410.\n- Genes with their own M below 0.5: 8. These are SDHA, HTATSF1, CDC40, RPL13a, CSNK2A2, AP3D1, UBC and PAK1IP1. The tool metric of 14 counts set sizes with average M below 0.5, not genes.\n- V2/3 = 0.0686. This is below 0.15, so two genes add little more.\n\n**NormFinder (stability value, lower is more stable)**\n- No groups: most stable AP3D1 = 0.1348. Least stable HPRT1 = 0.4810.\n- Grouped by tissue: most stable UBC = 0.0810. Least stable B2M = 0.1805.\n\n**geNorm, head samples only (11 samples)**\n- Best pair: HTATSF1 and CDC40. Average M = 0.1142. V2/3 = 0.0359.\n\n**Amplification efficiency (dilution series, linear fit of Cq against log10 molecules, 8 levels unless noted)**\n\n| Gene | Slope | Efficiency | Efficiency (%) | R² |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GAPDH | -3.4557 | 1.947 | 94.7 | 0.9987 |\n| HTATSF1 | -3.1799 | 2.063 | 106.3 | 0.9981 |\n| CDC40 | -3.2067 | 2.050 | 105.0 | 0.9986 |\n| RPL13a | -3.2923 | 2.013 | 101.3 | 0.9987 |\n| CSNK2A2 (6 levels) | -3.2359 | 2.037 | 103.7 | 0.9969 |\n| AP3D1 | -3.2235 | 2.043 | 104.3 | 0.9989 |\n| HPRT1 | -3.2105 | 2.049 | 104.9 | 0.9976 |\n| CYC1 (7 levels) | -3.4611 | 1.945 | 94.5 | 0.9987 |\n| EIF4A | -3.2491 | 2.031 | 103.1 | 0.9985 |\n| UBC (7 levels) | -3.3788 | 1.977 | 97.7 | 0.9924 |\n| PAK1IP1 | -3.2935 | 2.012 | 101.2 | 0.9996 |\n| ActB (named ACTB in file) | -3.2993 | 2.010 | 101.0 | 0.9986 |\n| 18S | -3.4209 | 1.960 | 96.0 | 0.9985 |\n| SDHA | -3.2331 | 2.038 | 103.8 | 0.9979 |\n\n- B2M is not in the dilution file. It has no efficiency value.\n- The fitted efficiencies range from 94.5 percent to 106.3 percent.\n\n**Uncertain**\n- The stability ranking used efficiency 2 for every gene. The fitted efficiencies are not used in that ranking. The tool did not rerun with them.\n- The two methods agree on HTATSF1 and CDC40 as the best pair. Both agree that B2M and HPRT1 are the least stable genes.\n- The methods disagree on the most stable single gene: AP3D1 without groups, UBC with tissue groups.\n- The head-only geNorm and the tissue-grouped NormFinder rest on small groups (11 and 9 samples in two of the groups).\n\n**Waiting for you**\n- Choose the reference genes. The analysis does not select them.\n- Decide whether to rerun the stability ranking with the fitted efficiencies.\n- Decide whether the 7 per-gene outlier flags in the head group need a check of the raw wells.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n5 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/hildyard2021-embryo-refgenes/run1/home/sessions/20261008-232410-da6e/work and wrote 0 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/hildyard2021-embryo-refgenes/run1/home/sessions/20261008-232410-da6e/work.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Amplification efficiencies: 2 · Technical replicates: mean · Wells that you exclude: none · Highest Cq that counts as detected: 40 · Column of the groups for NormFinder: .",
